WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.124 --> 00:00:17.608
Back in town the statue was also staring at something.

2
00:00:18.848 --> 00:00:22.089
He had no choice but to stare at the town all day.

3
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:26.210
His body was frozen in place.

4
00:00:27.511 --> 00:00:32.012
But he was alive inside his golden shell, watching people pass by.

5
00:00:34.268 --> 00:00:38.432
"Nana will pay for what's she done to me," he thought angrily.

6
00:00:38.452 --> 00:00:41.955
"If I ever escape this statue, that is!"

7
00:00:45.898 --> 00:00:49.201
One morning a group of townspeople began gathering at his base.

8
00:00:49.221 --> 00:00:52.384
"Here they are again!"

9
00:00:52.904 --> 00:00:54.546
the statue thought in frustration.

10
00:00:54.566 --> 00:00:57.989
"Every day they come and stand by me.

11
00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.592
And all they do is talk, talk, talk!

12
00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:06.758
Grr! I wish I had some fruit to throw at them!"

13
00:01:09.679 --> 00:01:13.200
Usually, the townspeople talked about how proud they were of the statue.

14
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.402
"His gold shines!"

15
00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:21.804
"His jewels sparkle!"

16
00:01:21.824 --> 00:01:25.526
"Look at his smile.

17
00:01:27.026 --> 00:01:29.267
Seeing him makes me happy too!"

18
00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:34.493
But this day was different.

19
00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:38.036
People weren't talking about the statue's smile.

20
00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:41.319
They weren't admiring his gold or jewels.

21
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.862
They were complaining—a lot!

22
00:01:44.882 --> 00:01:50.087
"I lost my farm," one man said.

23
00:01:50.107 --> 00:01:53.690
"I couldn't pay my taxes to the king."

24
00:01:53.710 --> 00:02:00.055
"I had to sell my shoes to buy food," a woman said.

25
00:02:02.076 --> 00:02:03.918
Others began calling out their problems.

26
00:02:05.339 --> 00:02:09.141
And reader, they had a lot of serious problems.

27
00:02:09.301 --> 00:02:12.664
"Grr," the statue thought.

28
00:02:12.684 --> 00:02:18.048
"If I could move my hands, I'd put them over my ears!"

29
00:02:20.009 --> 00:02:21.010
But he couldn't move.

30
00:02:22.211 --> 00:02:24.172
So, he had no choice but to listen.

31
00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:29.316
Soon the mayor arrived and quieted the crowd.

32
00:02:30.556 --> 00:02:32.277
"Why are you complaining?

33
00:02:32.297 --> 00:02:37.138
It was good of the king to give us this beautiful statue."

34
00:02:37.158 --> 00:02:41.739
"Exactly!" the statue thought.

35
00:02:41.759 --> 00:02:45.740
"I make this ugly town much prettier!"

36
00:02:48.141 --> 00:02:51.622
But then a girl, not much older than the prince, spoke up.

37
00:02:51.642 --> 00:02:54.222
"We like the statue.

38
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:56.323
But it's not a person.

39
00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.524
Why does it need all that gold?"

40
00:03:01.768 --> 00:03:05.150
"Its beauty doesn't help the poor," a woman added.

41
00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:10.613
"We could buy a lot of food with those jewels!"

42
00:03:11.213 --> 00:03:12.034
somebody shouted.

43
00:03:14.315 --> 00:03:15.236
The girl nodded.

44
00:03:15.256 --> 00:03:20.139
"What good is beauty if we're poor and hungry?"

45
00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:25.101
The statue wanted to stay angry.

46
00:03:26.362 --> 00:03:29.464
But he was beginning to feel something strange and new.

47
00:03:31.084 --> 00:03:34.225
"My chest feels funny," he thought.

48
00:03:36.246 --> 00:03:38.367
Then he remembered something Nana had said.

49
00:03:38.387 --> 00:03:41.928
"Your heart is as cold and heavy as stone."

50
00:03:41.948 --> 00:03:47.670
"It's my heart," the statue realized.

51
00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.771
"Nana was right.

52
00:03:52.111 --> 00:03:54.752
I have a cold and heavy heart."
